A||||42||TRiAD||PLEASE be seriously careful...||||4||
Z||000000||TRiAD||06-13-2001||07:59 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.khnl.com/Global/story.asp?S=364272" TARGET=_blank>http://www.khnl.com/Global/story.asp?S=364272</A> <BR>(newscast video included)<BR>Acura vs. Jetta street race that ended in a split-in-two Acura, and ended the 19-year-old driver's life. <P>25ft grind on a guardrail, 20+ft fall into a parking lot, long slid into a pole, and split in two. <P>We don't all know eachother personally here, but it kills me to hear stories like this...<P>Keep it on the track. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Tweek||06-13-2001||08:35 PM||||Wow, Im not gonna tell anyone to not street race cause there is no way I can stop you, but PLEASE be carefull, I took the liberty of copying a few pics from the video broadcast.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/Misc/crash1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/Misc/crash2.jpg"> <P>In the next one you can see the overpass guardrail he slid on, then fell off, and the missing signpost from where he went through it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/Misc/crash3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/Misc/crash4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/Misc/crash5.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Tweek (edited 06-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||06-13-2001||09:08 PM||||a moment of silence...    ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Homicidal||06-13-2001||09:18 PM||||*breaks silence*<P>GOD DAMN!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<P>Racing = stupidity, sorry.  My heart goes out, but not much when people bring this sort of ****  upon themselves.<P>------------------<BR><B>It's sad, in the 20th Century, in the 1990's, we would have to still go the same bullshit route<BR>that artists have to go, to get acceptance.  If it wasn't for the independence, if it wasn't for the <BR>small little cities, and the few little ghetto guys, trying to make music, it never would have happened.<BR>Some of these guys will never make a dime, some of thse guys will be poor and die, alone.  <P>But in the proccess, they've been the true renegades.<P>And the true rebels always walk alone anyways.</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||beer_stud_21||06-13-2001||09:41 PM||||Thats a mean wreck.  I didn't hear about it on the news here locally.  Must have missed it.  Oahu has a lot of bad traffic accidents.  Crazy drivers over there.  I've only been over there a little bit but I saw enough to make me never want to live there.   Just a few months ago they had a drunk off duty police officer run a red light and t-bone a 19 yr old girl coming home from work (killed her).  Then the other day I read about a 19 yr old kid that got killed here on the big island not 10 miles from my house when he was street racing and rear ended the toyota he was racing at something like 85mph.  Went sideways and hit a tree.  Killed him and injured his gf i believe and both people in the toyota.  (it flipped)  Its really scary how many guys my age around here have the racing mentality.  Everyone jokes about beating those slow hondas but maybe we shouldn't encourage them.  <P>drive safe.<BR>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000005||fyerstarter||06-13-2001||10:53 PM||||Hopefully all the people who responded in the street racing thread a week ago with "I dont care what anyone says, I will always street race. If I die I die happy" will reconsider. There is a time and place for everything. But this just isn't it. <P>And I'm sure there are some people who will say "That kid got killed because he didn't know how to drive right, he's just some punk rice boy was probably fiddling with his radio", I'm a better driver than that". <P>How naive are you?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bill H||06-13-2001||11:53 PM||||In responce to the racing thread where it was stated "if i die i die happy" It might not be yourself that you end up killing. Moral when in doubt Back Off and be safe. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Maniak84||06-14-2001||12:27 AM||||i like those wheels on the blue car do anybody make those that fit an 84 fiero||||reg||1
Z||000008||pontiacs4me||06-14-2001||02:39 AM||||and cell phones, enough said.||||reg||1
Z||000009||84Bill||06-14-2001||09:13 AM||||Thats just plain scary to look at. In all my years I have never seen a car so completly destroyed. Sure glad no one else was hurt by this idiots debris raining down all over the place. If he did DIE happy I don't know how with SH!T in his pants. I feel sorry for his parents and family. There is a special playground where you can do this stuff safely, It's called a drag track! or Raceway! I can see how a small mind can confuse Highway with Raceway. <BR>It's one thing on an empty back road or empty open highway with limited access but in a dence populated area is just plain stupid! I hope no one in this area ever kills one of my family members by doing this, I'm a very patient man, rest assured vengence will be mine.||||reg||11
Z||000010||Galen||06-14-2001||09:26 AM||||I'll streetrace all the same as always. This will change opinion none, Death happens. yeah it sucks that it does. but oh well.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>  -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-14-2001||09:37 AM||||a grim reminder that our cars are 90% steel<P>and we are 90% water<P>I have nothing against racing cars if you want to put your life on the line, everything we do has some degree of risk to it.<P> racing on an overpass appears to be potentially fatal.<P> here in western NY you can take your car to Lancaster speedway, I think on friday or saturday nights, and with a minimum amount of requirements you can drag race anyone you want on the 1/4 mile<P>  and with a little more investment you can easily get into the weekly stock or modified stock car races.<P>  this reminds me of the end of American Grafitti, where Harrison Ford rolls the chevy. back then people had the smarts to fart around in the city, and to do the serious stuff out on the edge of town.<P>  but on an overpass or a bridge, geeze!||||reg||1
Z||000012||KRMFiero||06-14-2001||10:02 AM||||That's horrible... There is nothing wrong with racing as long as:<BR>1. Your car can handle it<BR>2. You can handle it<BR>3. it is in a safe place with no padestrians, not many turns and nothing on side of road for you to hit  - basically eather I-95 if no one/not many people are on it OR a race track<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Justin||06-14-2001||10:07 AM||||It's all for the rush.  Drag racing is fun, but when your out on the street and some guy revs up his car, and you know you can take him, you want to race.  This is where the line divides the people.  Some people will say, well, it's not worth it, why put my life on the line to race somebody?  Other will say, well, I'm only gonna live once, so I might as well have fun.  And they don't think they will die because nothing like that can happen to them.  And nothing anybody can say or do will change thier mind.  They have to find out for themselves, and by that time, it may be too late.  This is the sad thing.<P>------------------<BR>If at first you don't succeed, pretend you were never trying in the first place.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.plauder-smilies.de/rough/greenchainsaw.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||84Bill||06-14-2001||10:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>I'll streetrace all the same as always. This will change opinion none, Death happens. yeah it sucks that it does. but oh well.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>May 1000 tickets plague your future, I hope you die a lonely death.||||reg||14
Z||000015||DRH||06-14-2001||10:54 AM||||I am a firm believer in a person's right to risk their own life. I don't care much for mandatory seatbelt or motorcycle helmet laws that apply to adults.<P>However, you shouldn't put other people at undue risk. That's the problem with red light street racing... the adrenaline gets going and people don't take the time to think about what COULD happen. Imagine someone driving (or worse walking) in that parking lot when a ton and a half of steel came flying from above at 100 MPH.<P>If you can't keep it on the track, at least go somewhere that you and your competitor are the only people at risk.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||drednot||06-14-2001||11:16 AM||||That Acura Integra was structurally weak.  Rice is not safe.  This is not the first time I have scene an Acura Integra split in half <BR>Here are some real life accidents including another chopped Integra--<P><BR>two.http://towzone.com/roadkill.html<P>If My X-Frame Impala hit that sign @ 100 mhp, the sign would have been long gone.  I don't have to worry about it going 100 mph though, it only has a 283.  I do race, and I still will.  I just won't do it on un-familiar roads.  There is a time and place for everything.  Racing is Dangerous, no doubt about that.  If you believe that your risks are minimal, you are at a place you know, and you won't get crazy to win, I find it acceptable. <P>||||reg||11
Z||000017||drednot||06-14-2001||11:18 AM||||Wrong address, here is the right one<P> <A HREF="http://towzone.com/roadkill.html" TARGET=_blank>http://towzone.com/roadkill.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||ferg||06-14-2001||11:25 AM||||I feel bad for that kids parents. I wouldn't wish that call on anyone.<P>But on a lighter note...<P>How long do you think his buddies waited until they tried to strip the car for parts- his misfortune is his friends gain.||||reg||1
