Z||000025||84Bill||06-14-2001||04:01 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B> blah blah blah, thats real manly of you to wish death on someone becuz of a opinion. I bet you get all the 80 yearold chics when you go crusing at the retirement homes dont ya?<P>As for whoeever it was that was talking about walking out in front of someone going 100mph.. whats the differant between walking out in front of someone going 10-15? yeah they have more time to stop, but not if they arn't paying attention.. yup I can see me now "Oh look, there is a car driving like a maniac doing over 100mph, I had better walk out in front of him to slow him down so he doesn't hurt himself. ouch, He has hit me, look at me flying through the air. Better aim for that big car there to break my fall. Ouch again, that big car hurt. I'm dead, woe is me"<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm sorry pea brained twit but perhaps I shoud break it down a bit so it can all fit in that puny little dingelburry you call a head.<BR>what I ment was I hope you don't kill anyone else by continuing you stupid little fits of ignorant bliss you call street racing. there are individuals in this scociety that cant see all that well and will pull out in front of you because their depth perception is not what it used to be not to mention their judgement of speed has set through many years of driving around under normal conditions. <BR>A car traveling at 100 mph covers a lot of distance in a short amount of time, to an unweary eye it looks like a normal car from 400 yards away. And just in the event you have not noticed,  kids never look when running out into streets. I'm sure this makes no sense to you and I'm sure you really don't care and in that case I can only wish for poetic justice. Have a pleasent day idiot!<P>I'm sure glad I paid to do this.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||Galen||06-14-2001||08:20 PM||||ahhh.. you unruley soul you..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe. if you must know, yes I have 'run over' someone before. hehe, scared the living shittles out of me. In a fiero at that, I tried to pin my brother between the back & a brick wall. <P>pea brained? idiot? hehe, now now, you dont have to resort to childish angst to insult me, be a man, and shut up. Who ever said anything about racing in a parking lot anyways? "Come on boys, we gonna go street racing in a parking lot. See how many old fogeys we can get this time. Yeeeehawwww.." Grow up.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>  -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
Z||000027||84Bill||06-14-2001||08:48 PM||||Gaylen do you like to pull the wings off flies and still burn ants with a magnifieing glass? Did mommy and daddy not love you enough? Grow up? heh yeah that good. Must have hurt to come up with that one. Shut up? I can assure you you will never hear me utter a word. ||||reg||1
Z||000028||DRH||06-14-2001||09:39 PM||||Galen,<P>I'm the one that mentioned walking etc... It was in reference to THIS wreck... LOOK AT THE PICTURES... If someone were walking thru that parking lot or down the cross street, they WOULD NOT have stepped out in front of a car doing 100... They would have had a car doing 100 fly at them from above. I don't know about you but I don't generally look for cars flying off of overpasses before walking across a parking lot. If the car was doing 15 it never would have jumped the guard rail to begin with.<P>The people racing in this story didn't say "let's go race in a parking lot..." either but one of them damn sure wound up flying through one. It's just luck that he didn't kill an old fogey, or even a young one. The point is you should think about what COULD happen... not just what you plan to happen.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Greg Piet||06-14-2001||10:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>That's horrible... There is nothing wrong with racing as long as:<BR>1. Your car can handle it<BR>2. You can handle it<BR>3. it is in a safe place with no padestrians, not many turns and nothing on side of road for you to hit  - basically eather I-95 if no one/not many people are on it OR a race track<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not many turns???<BR>I cant stand straight line racing, but then again if one is going to race...<BR>Test and Tune dragracing and Autocrossing is DIRT CHEAP and a lot safer!!!!!!<P><P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 SM<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">    <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
