Z||000032||Black88GT||06-16-2001||08:55 PM||||Geesh 84Bill, maybe you should discuss your hostility with your psychiatrist, and while your there refill your Prozac prescription.<P>Of the one or two stories you hear annually about street racing casualties, there are millions and millions of other street races that turn out just fine.  I see atleast 1 or 2 races just driving to work on a daily basis.  Going out on the weekends I see between 5-10.<P>Those of you who say "Take it to the track", well the closest track to me is a good 45 min. drive.  Its so busy that you would be lucky to get 2 runs over a 6 hour time period.  I don't have the time nor the gas money for that every time I want to race my car. <P>If you think that these stories on the news are what happens all the time in street racing, well then you are the one who is being naive.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||4
Z||000033||TRiAD||06-16-2001||09:06 PM||||I think anyone in large cities on the west coast in particular can tell you there are more than 2 deaths a year due to this ignorant and irresponsible crap. <P>I've seen posts on other threads where people relate more than 2 in a weekend in one town! (other people back it up with "yeah, I saw that on the news/in the paper..."). <P>It's real simple. You have <B>no right</B> to endanger others for your entertainment. Period. <P>As for the closest track, being in Baltimore, I seriously doubt there are none within 45 minutes, try looking for autocross clubs, it's more challanging than "point and shoot" drags anyway. <BR>If the tracks near you are real busy, all the more reason to support them...they'll have to make more, and maybe one will be closer to you! I think it was San Francisco where they were building more and more 1/4 drags to try and keep it off the road. <P>Anyway, the point is, you're affecting other people, and if you can't realize that (or worse...don't care), then you have no business on our roads. ||||reg||1
Z||000034||JSocha||06-16-2001||09:06 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Hmmmm?  I just wonder if he was wearing his seatbelt...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000035||Black88GT||06-16-2001||09:33 PM||||OK, its me lined up against someone else at a light.  1 in the morning, no other cars around or people.  I am endangering .... ?<P>Also, the closest track is 45 min. away, Cecil County Raceway.  The next closest to that is about 90 min. away.  The closest Auto X club, AutoCrossers Inc., is 30 min. away.  Also, I like drag racing better anyway.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000036||Sleeper||06-17-2001||01:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>I think anyone in large cities on the west coast in particular can tell you there are more than 2 deaths a year due to this ignorant and irresponsible crap. <P>I've seen posts on other threads where people relate more than 2 in a weekend in one town! (other people back it up with "yeah, I saw that on the news/in the paper..."). <P>It's real simple. You have [b]no right</B> to endanger others for your entertainment. Period. <P>As for the closest track, being in Baltimore, I seriously doubt there are none within 45 minutes, try looking for autocross clubs, it's more challanging than "point and shoot" drags anyway. <BR>If the tracks near you are real busy, all the more reason to support them...they'll have to make more, and maybe one will be closer to you! I think it was San Francisco where they were building more and more 1/4 drags to try and keep it off the road. <P>Anyway, the point is, you're affecting other people, and if you can't realize that (or worse...don't care), then you have no business on our roads. [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>i'm here on the west coast, there are street racing wrecks all the time. sometime you'll hear about it and sometimes you won't. sometimes ppl die and sometimes they don't. this wreck here is pretty nasty, God only knows if he had a cage...<P>"Keep it off the Streets"  the R.A.S.R motto. bullshit. there are only two dragstrips left in LA county, one is about an hour away and the other is 2 hours. at one time there was like five but now only two remain because of deaths and noise to the other three. and Pomona the closest one i hear there are rumors of closing that one up too because of noisiness so...streetracing is life to some ppl/kids over here cuz the cities have took the dragstrips away from us.<P>keep it on the streets -- its where it begun. if some fool drowns at the beach are you not going to go in the water anymore? come on.||||reg||1
Z||000037||Tigger||06-17-2001||01:39 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>OK, its me lined up against someone else at a light.  1 in the morning, no other cars around or people.  I am endangering .... ?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>Also, the closest track is 45 min. away, Cecil County Raceway.  The next closest to that is about 90 min. away.  The closest Auto X club, AutoCrossers Inc., is 30 min. away.  Also, I like drag racing better anyway.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Whaa waa...  I know guys that drive or trailer a car all over the country to race at drag strips.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Originally posted by Sleeper:<BR>keep it on the streets -- its where it begun.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL, ya like, keep'in it real.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-17-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000038||84Bill||06-17-2001||12:12 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Geesh 84Bill, maybe you should discuss your hostility with your psychiatrist, and while your there refill your Prozac prescription. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You know nothing about me other than I have an extreme dislike for people that do really dumb stuff like the individual above. Perhaps you should discuss you suicidal tendencies with a shrink if you like to street race   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Of the one or two stories you hear annually about street racing casualties, there are millions and millions of other street races that turn out just fine.  I see at least 1 or 2 races just driving to work on a daily basis.  Going out on the weekends I see between 5-10. </B> <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank god for that!<P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Those of you who say "Take it to the track", well the closest track to me is a good 45 min. drive.  Its so busy that you would be lucky to get 2 runs over a 6 hour time period.  I don't have the time nor the gas money for that every time I want to race my car. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I drove my 79 camaro 50 miles one way nearly every weekend to race it. I made quite a few friends waiting in line and that was 1/2 the fun the other 1/4 of the time was gawking at the mini car show.<BR>It was no sweat for me to do that considering Russian roulette is an uncool game. <P><BR><B>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>If you think that these stories on the news are what happens all the time in street racing, well then you are the one who is being naive.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I could care less if it happens every day, all I'm saying is keep me out of your silly games. If one of you fools out the kills one of my family members while playing "lets see who is faster" I have a problem with that. I don't have a problem with street racing as long as it does not involve me or my family and it's done in a well suited area. Not in the down town area like this fool.<P>The idiot above died alone and that's about the only good thing that resulted from this tragedy<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-17-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000039||Tweek||06-17-2001||12:34 PM||||Now I am speaking in general terms... so don't point the flamethrower this way because I am not talking about any 1 person and not everybody falls in the categories...<BR>That said.<P>Why does it seems that most street racing is done by adolescents with too much testosterone, that need to prove that they are better than everyone else.<P>Whereas track/autocrossing tends to be done by adults who are serious about their sport, and just want to have a good time doing it.||||reg||1
Z||000040||Toddster||06-17-2001||01:05 PM||||I am certainly not the pot to call the kettle black. I did my fair share of drag racing in my youth and I still like to put the occassional Rice Rocket in his place. BUT...<P>I always exercised reasonable prudence. I raced on 6 lane highways at 6:00am on a sunday, I raced on lonely stretches of road with no housing or parks or hidden entrances, I had a 5 point racing harness on and I KNEW my limits.<P>what was this idiot thinking? In front of a mall? on a busy road?<P>All you youngsters out there in Fiero-land. I'm not going to tell you not to do something I've done. Just use some common sense and let this Darwin Award Candidate's death be a lesson.||||reg||1
